  "figure": {
    "id": "fig09",
    "number": "9",
    "title": "Effect of sweep angle on the variation of drag coefficient at zero lift with Mach number for the wing-body configuration.",
    "pdf_page": 31,
    "printed_page": 29,
    "x_axis": "Mach number, M (grid 0.40 to 1.20 by 0.05; frame lines at 0.40 and 1.20)",
    "y_axis": "C_D0, drag coefficient at zero lift (grid 0 to 0.030 by 0.005; frame lines at 0 and 0.030)",
    "content_note": "Three faired curves without symbols, for sweep 10.8, 35 and 47 deg. Line identity read by tracing: below M = 0.82 the 35 deg curve is the middle of the three lines (below the 10.8 deg line, above the 47 deg line), crosses the CD0 = 0.010 grid line near M = 0.79 and runs along it from about M = 0.65 to 0.81; from about M = 0.83 to 0.87 it lies alongside the 10.8 deg line as one two-stroke band (band width never drops to a single stroke, so the lines do not cross; 35 deg is the lower stroke); from M = 0.88 it is the middle curve of the transonic rise (legend '35' sits at the right end of this middle curve). It is solid to M = 1.037, dashed from M = 1.04 to 1.081 (three short dashes, level near CD0 = 0.0200), absent between M = 1.081 and 1.088, and solid again from M = 1.088 to 1.131 (a single long stroke, about 0.043 in M, falling to the right; read as the faired line through the supersonic points, unlike the short dashes before it). Sample M = 1.085 is left out: its column (about x = 2394 px) falls in the gap between the last dash (ends x = 2385) and the start of the final solid stroke (x = 2404, M = 1.088). Cross-check of line identity against figure 6(b) (35 deg polars, my own rough reading, not part of this result): the M = 0.50 faired polar crosses CL = 0 at CD about 0.0090 and the M = 0.70 polar at about 0.0099, closer to the middle line (0.0096, 0.0100) than to the upper line (0.0102, 0.0103); the M = 0.90 polar gives about 0.011, matching the middle curve there."
  },
